# Requests you can send from Visual Studio: open this file and click "Send request" above a request.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Supported currencies
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reference/currencies

### Unknown route -> 404 ProblemDetails
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/does-not-exist

### OpenAPI document (Development only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Customers (start the database first: docker compose up -d --wait)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Register a customer -> 201 Created + Location
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Ali",
  "lastName": "Yılmaz",
  "nationalId": "10000000146",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-05-20",
  "email": "ali@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+905321234567"
}

### Read the customer just registered (uses the id from the "register" response) -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/{{register.response.body.$.id}}

### Same national id again -> 409 Customers.NationalIdAlreadyRegistered
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Ayşe",
  "lastName": "Kaya",
  "nationalId": "10000000146",
  "dateOfBirth": "1985-03-10",
  "email": "ayse@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+905331112233"
}

### Missing fields -> 400 with an "errors" entry per field
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Ali"
}

### Wrong TCKN checksum -> 400 Customers.InvalidNationalId
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Can",
  "lastName": "Demir",
  "nationalId": "12345678901",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-05-20",
  "email": "can@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+905321234567"
}

### Under 18 -> 422 Customers.Underage
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Deniz",
  "lastName": "Ak",
  "nationalId": "12345678950",
  "dateOfBirth": "2015-01-01",
  "email": "deniz@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+905321234567"
}

### Unknown customer -> 404 Customers.NotFound
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/01a10d01-0000-7000-8000-000000000000
